@@ -14,6 +14,35 @@ The sections up to "On Linux" are the macOS window's, AppKit's. "On Linux"
 is the window on Linux, SDL3's on Wayland or X11, entry by entry against
 them; its `manual` checks are on a Linux host's guest boot.
 
+## Experimental captured desktop input on Linux
+
+- Captured desktop motion uses the host acceleration curve; callers may override
+  it with `SDL_MOUSE_RELATIVE_SYSTEM_SCALE=0` for raw input. `manual`
+
+- A host supplying `relative_pointer` opts into SDL relative capture. The capture
+  click establishes an absolute position; later motion and button changes use
+  relative input, permitting one guest cursor to cross guest display boundaries
+  while keyboard focus stays with the capturing host window. Release and focus
+  loss lift held buttons. Other hosts ignore this callback.
+  `test: native::linux::input::relative_capture_preserves_motion_buttons_and_release`
+- Without a host-cursor layout socket, cursor capabilities are disabled so the
+  guest draws its own cursor in the framebuffer; the host cursor is hidden over
+  the image. Software cursor fallback and physical border crossing need a guest
+  boot check. `manual`
+
+- `REIMS_VGPU_HOST_CURSOR_SOCKET` opts into a local cursor prototype. The private
+  stream receives the companion's display bounds. Captured motion follows that
+  arrangement, scaled by the destination window's image; pointer coordinates and
+  local cursor placement use the same wire quantization.
+  `test: native::linux::desktop_pointer::displayed_coordinates_match_wire_quantization`
+- Local routing crosses touching guest bounds and slides along walls without
+  jumping gaps. `test: native::linux::desktop_pointer::gaps_stop_and_walls_slide`
+- The local cursor uses a transparent, noninteractive SDL child surface, separate
+  from guest Vulkan frames. Guest cursor capabilities remain enabled. Transport
+  loss or a changed layout releases capture and held input. Visibility, cursor
+  shapes, click alignment, resize scaling and physical latency require a VM boot.
+  This is an unaccepted prototype. `manual`
+
 ## Switches
 
